Source: https://github.com/spf13/cobra/blob/main/site/content/user_guide.md

Cobra commands support PreRun and PostRun hooks that execute before or after the main Run function. PersistentPreRun and PersistentPostRun hooks are inherited by child commands if they don't define their own. The execution order for hooks is PersistentPreRun, PreRun, Run, PostRun, PersistentPostRun. By default, only the first persistent hook in the chain is executed; setting EnableTraverseRunHooks to true executes all parent persistent hooks.

